{title: How the Mighty Have Fallen}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 14:49; 31:1–2; 2 Samuel 1:17–27; 1 Samuel 31:8–10; 31:11–13; 1 Chronicles 8:33}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Ner fathered Kish, and Kish fathered [B]Saul
Saul fathered Jonathan, [G#m]Malchishua, Abinadab
[D#m]The genealogy stands in the book of [B]Chronicles
List[G#m]ing the sons who served in the [D#m]land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
How the mighty have fall[B]en
Your glory lies slain on your [G#m]heights
The shield of the mighty is de[A#7]filed
No longer anoin[D#m]ted with oil
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The Philistines closed in on [B]the king
They struck down Jonathan and [G#m]Abinadab
Mal-chi-shua fell with [D#m]his father
On the slopes of Mount Gilboa
Many fell slain as the Israelites [B]fled
Before the closing in of the ene[G#m]my
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
How the mighty have [D#m]fallen
Your glory lies [B]slain on your heights
The [G#m]shield of the mighty is defiled
[D#m]No longer anointed with oil
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
They cut off his head and stripped his armor
[B]Sent word to the temples of idols
They put his [G#m]armor in the house of Ashtoreth
[D#m]Fastened his body to the wall of Beth-shan
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
But the people of Ja-besh-gi-lead heard
All their fighting [B]men set out by night
They took the [G#m]bodies down from the wall
[D#m]Brought them to Jabesh and burned them there
They took the bones and buried them
[B]Under the tamarisk tree at Jabesh
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G#m]How the mighty have fall[D#m]en
Your glory lies slain [B]on your heights
The shield [G#m]of the mighty is defiled
No [D#m]longer anointed with oil
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [B] | [G#m] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Outro}
They fasted seven days for Saul
And for his sons [B]who did not return [D#m]
{end_of_verse}
